==Porting to a new architecture==

See [[Porting ERIKA Enterprise and RT-Druid to a new microcontroller]] for the general instructions.

# Create the architecture-specific directory <tt>ee/pkg/cpu/XXX</tt>
# Create the files <tt>inc/ee_cpu.h</tt> and <tt>inc/ee_internal.h</tt> in the above directory.  They should include all the files <tt>cpu/common/inc/ee_*.h</tt> suitable for your architecture.  Write any architecture-specific definition or declaration in them.
# Modify the files <tt>ee/pkg/ee.h</tt> and <tt>ee/pkg/ee_internal.h</tt> to include your newly create files.
# Modify the file <tt>cpu/common/cfg/cfg.mk</tt> to compile the common C source files suitable for your architecture.
# Create or modify any additional file you need.
# Run <tt>make</tt> and enjoy.

